{
 "_note": "Shared worked-example data for FMS engineering item 8 (module library: complete circuits per module): guide docs/FMS system design/68_module_circuits.md, tools/fmse/*.py, web/fmse8*.js. One circuit LIBRARY: standard circuit patterns + every module M01-M22 as a list of pattern instances. All derived lists (IO list, IO cards, addresses, terminals, cables, BOM, power, 24 V) are computed from it with the rules below - guide, tools and web must give IDENTICAL results. All values are EXAMPLES; real circuits are designed and signed off by qualified electrical / safety engineers to IEC 60204-1 and the current standards. Item 7 gives the principles and sizing formulas. REVISION 2026-11-15: per-instance power cable sizing (rule power_cable) and ZONE_OUT safety outputs on M18 (rule zone_out).",
 "_rules": {
  "expand": "For a module: walk its instances in list order. Each instance contributes the pattern's io, dev and cab entries in pattern order. Module instance unit = UNIT code + '01' (one module of the type; in a kit the number counts up per module code, like item 5/6).",
  "tag": "tag = site.area.cell.unit.group.signal = 'PLT1.MACH.FMS1.' + unit + '.' + group + '.' + signal (item-5 rule, max 48 characters).",
  "designation": "device designation (IEC 81346): class code from the pattern dev entry + running number per class code inside the module in expansion order (FC1, FC2 ..., QA1 ..., BG1 ...). Full: '=FMS1.' + unit + '-' + class + n. Cables: 'WD' + running number in expansion order. Class letters (IEC 81346-2, check your edition): BG position/presence sensing, BP pressure, BT temperature, EB heating, FC over-current protection, KF electrical signal processing, MA electric motor, MB solenoid, PF visual indicator / HMI, QA power switching (contactor, breaker), SF manual control (push-button, switch), TA inverter / converter (AC/AC), TB AC/DC or DC/DC converter (power supply, UPS), WD cable, XD terminal.",
  "io_cards": "IO types and channels per card (example ET 200SP-class sizes): DI 16, DO 16, AI 4, AO 2, FDI 8, FDO 4. used(type) = number of io entries of that type. cards(type) = 0 if used = 0 else ceil(used*(1 + reserve)/channels) with reserve = 0.2. spare(type) = cards*channels - used. Addresses: the k-th io entry of a type (k = 0,1,... in expansion order) gets card = k // channels + 1, channel = k % channels, written TYPE + card + '.' + channel with 2 digits, e.g. DI1.00, FDI2.07.",
  "station": "a module with at least one io entry gets an IO station (bus interface + cards): i24 = 0.3 + 0.05*cards_total ; loss = 4 + 1*cards_total [W] ; BOM: 'IO station bus interface' 1 + each card type count ('DI 16 card' ...).",
  "terminals": "control terminal strip -XD2: terminals = number of io entries + sum of the pattern 'tx' extras (supply terminals +24 V / 0 V for field devices) of all instances; numbered 1..n in expansion order (io first then extras of the same instance).",
  "cables": "one cable per pattern 'cab' entry, length = default length (instance parameter 'len' overrides all cables of the instance - not used in this library). Totals: number of cables, total metres, metres per cores text.",
  "bom": "BOM = count of each 'BOM item' text over all dev entries + station items + 24 V PSU ('24 V power supply <rating> A') + 'Control terminal' x terminals; sorted by item text.",
  "motor": "per DOL / VFD_STO instance: kW from params ; eta = 0.88, cos = 0.82 unless given ; In = kW*1000/(sqrt(3)*400*eta*cos) ; DOL: contactor = smallest of contactor_ac3 >= In ; MPCB setting = In (round 2) ; VFD: inverter size = smallest of vfd_kw >= kW ; loss VFD = 0.03*kW*1000 W ('3%').",
  "power": "module load list (item 7 formulas with ks = 1): loads = FEEDER_EXT (kW, ku, cos from params), DOL and VFD_STO motors (kW, ku = 0.7, cos = 0.82 unless given), HEATER (kW, ku = 0.8, cos = 1.0), plus control power = PSU rating*24/0.9/1000 kW with ku 0.6, cos 0.95 (only if PSU > 0). P = sum kW*ku ; Q = sum P_i*tan(acos(cos_i)) ; S = sqrt(P^2+Q^2) ; I = S*1000/(sqrt(3)*400) (demand - used for the cell load list). FEEDER sizing uses the installed rated values (ku = 1 for every load): P_inst = sum kW ; Q_inst = sum kW*tan(acos(cos)) ; S_inst = sqrt(P_inst^2 + Q_inst^2) ; I_inst = S_inst*1000/(sqrt(3)*400) ; feeder breaker In = smallest of breaker_ratings >= I_inst (Ib <= In as in item 7) ; cable = smallest ampacity-table size with Iz_table >= In/(k_temp*k_group) (item 7). A module with S_inst = 0 has no feeder (In 0, cable 0). Simplification: motor kW is used as electrical kW (efficiency neglected in the load list, only used for motor In).",
  "dc24": "module 24 V current = sum of pattern i24 over instances + station i24 ; PSU = smallest of psu_sizes >= current*1.25 (0 if current = 0).",
  "loss": "cabinet losses = sum of pattern losses (VFD 3 % of kW) + station loss + PSU loss (PSU rating*24*(1/0.92 - 1) W, 0 if no PSU).",
  "kit": "kit totals = sum over the modules of the kit (each module code may appear several times): io per type, cards per type, terminals, cables, metres, P, S, PSU sum, losses; kit IO tag list = each module instance with its own unit number. ROUNDING: module values are rounded first (P, S to 3 decimals, I to 2, loss to 1 decimal) and the kit totals add these rounded module values (like adding a printed schedule) -> kit S 132.682 kVA, loss 1251.6 W. Distribution-board feeder of a module instance: designation '=FMS1.' + unit + '-FC' + (number of FC devices of the module + 1).",
  "power_cable": "per instance of a pattern with 'pcab' (DOL, VFD_STO, HEATER, FEEDER_EXT) the power cable cores are sized from that instance (item 7 rule Ib <= Ip <= Iz*k): Ib = motor In (DOL / VFD_STO, motor rule) or kW*1000/(sqrt(3)*400*cos) (HEATER cos 1.0 unless given; FEEDER_EXT installed kW and cos from params, ku ignored) ; protective device current Ip = motor In (MPCB setting / inverter motor-overload setting = rated motor current) for DOL and VFD_STO, or the smallest of breaker_ratings >= Ib for HEATER and FEEDER_EXT ; A = smallest ampacity_table size with Iz_table >= Ip/(k_temp*k_group) (1.5 mm2 minimum = first row) ; cores text = prefix + A (no trailing .0, e.g. 4G2.5, 4G10) + suffix, replacing the pattern default text of cab entry 'index'. Results: Ib round 2, Ip (round 2 for motors), A. Lengths and cable counts are unchanged. This replaces the old fixed cores (gap found in guide 68 review: 18 kW heater had 4G2.5, 15 kW pump had 4G1.5).",
  "zone_out": "M18 SAFE01 carries the zone safety outputs: one ZONE_OUT instance per safety zone (library default Zone1..Zone4), each = 1 FDO (2-channel PM) + 1 FDI (EDM feedback). Gap fix: before, SAFE01 had no FDO."
 },
